KaiT2en-NixOS divergence: t2-power-tune never touches T2 vhci devices.

The wakeup and runtime-PM scan lists the devices behind the T2's
virtual USB host, apple-t2-vhci-hcd (internal keyboard, trackpad, Touch
Bar, the T2 NCM link). They are recognised by the auxiliary device the
bridge creates for it, apple_t2_bridge.vhci.N, in their sysfs path (the
same match t2-power-explorer uses). Disabling wakeup there removes the
machine's ability to wake itself: the next sleep is recoverable only by
plugging in AC, whose ACPI event still wakes the SoC. Excluded at scan time, in the saved-state filter, and
in validate() so the pkexec-ed helper also refuses them from stale or
crafted state. (Originally landed in-tree as 92d2a1b; moved here so
apps/ stays byte-identical to upstream. Rebased in the 2026-11-15 sync
from the t2bce_vhci class device onto the apple-t2-bridge one: without
that the exclusion silently matched nothing.)

Applied by apps/t2-power-tune/package.nix on top of the upstream
source (-p1 relative to apps/t2-power-tune).

Drop condition: remove when upstream t2-power-tune-helper excludes the
devices behind apple-t2-vhci-hcd (or all T2-internal devices) from the
wakeup and runtime-PM tunables, in scan() and validate(). Re-check
every sync.

